1d33e413d898" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321058 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321058 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35292" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321058 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321058 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the dimension of\n$\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321058 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8505e165-2993-5e50-9039-0c1c0e794caf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321058 #edb/ref 1074 "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 22 & -44 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{22}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 22 & -44 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321065 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321065 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321065 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321065 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321065 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2a41f8fd-4b7f-554c-b544-a6304735d193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321065 #edb/ref 1074 "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{5}{2} & 5 & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, \n$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\})=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345465 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345465 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345465 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e3095f8-ebd6-5417-b5fa-228deb53654e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345633 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345633 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345633 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1ffb8a8a-2e10-5113-8365-30ccd72226d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346122 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346122 #edb/ref 1082 #